97612	The compatibility contract adds one detached, bounded, exact-canonical
97613	bootstrap-operation policy value to recovery custody. Its frozen semantic name
97614	is `exactCanonicalPinnedGenesisBootstrapOperationBytes`. It is trusted local
97615	application policy, not a signed wire field, persisted control carrier, public
97616	room API, or statement that the creator observed the operation. The room must
97617	canonicalize a detached copy of `application.bootstrapOperation`, enforce the
97618	opened blueprint's existing operation-byte budget and the enclosing v3
97619	vertex's existing canonical depth/item/byte limits, and supply the same bytes
97620	to fresh recovery and cold successor reopen. Hot adoption copies those bytes
97621	from the source registration through sealed close facts and private successor
97622	live material without adding a new hot public input key. Private and closed
97623	input snapshots must copy rather than alias the bytes. The configured canonical
97624	value must be byte-stable for the same application, author, and object across
97625	process restart; a different application version or value is a fail-closed
97626	compatibility mismatch and stops for an explicit migration reslice rather than
97627	silently changing bootstrap authority. A caller that omits, mutates, supplies
97628	noncanonical/oversized bytes,
97629	or changes them across a successor boundary cannot obtain pinned-genesis
97630	bootstrap classification on a historical aggregate path. Existing recovery
97631	paths with no pinned-genesis row or no historical aggregate remain behaviorally
97632	unchanged. The field is optional in the exported TypeScript input so recovery
97633	that never needs a pinned-genesis row retains source compatibility, but it is
97634	mandatory at runtime for every pinned-genesis classification: absence returns
97635	the existing typed authentication/recovery refusal. No call may retain the
97636	current permissive predicate as a fallback. This optional-with-fail-closed-use
97637	rule is the frozen compatibility choice. Exact-record compatibility is frozen,
97638	not weakened: `recoverV3LiveReplica()` accepts exactly base keys, base plus
97639	`operationAdmissionPolicy`, base plus
97640	`exactCanonicalPinnedGenesisBootstrapOperationBytes`, or base plus both
97641	optional keys, and rejects every other extra key.
97642	`reopenCreatorSuccessorAdoption()` accepts exactly its existing 17 cold keys or
97643	those keys plus the bootstrap policy and rejects every other extra key. Its
97644	private `CreatorSuccessorReopenInput` mirrors the optional value. The existing
97645	six-key hot activation surface and the 11-key pending-recovery surface remain
97646	unchanged.
